WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.207
Art everywhere.

2
00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:04.154
People everywhere make art, and they always have.

3
00:00:04.314 --> 00:00:07.518
Someone painted animals on a cave wall thousands of years ago.

4
00:00:07.678 --> 00:00:09.211
Someone wove a basket.

5
00:00:09.371 --> 00:00:10.950
Someone carved a mask.

6
00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.385
Someone made a whole painting out of dots.

7
00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:15.728
Art is not only pictures in frames.

8
00:00:16.428 --> 00:00:17.728
Looking closely.

9
00:00:17.888 --> 00:00:19.978
To look at art, look for the parts.

10
00:00:20.138 --> 00:00:21.996
What lines did the artist make?

11
00:00:22.156 --> 00:00:23.224
What shapes?

12
00:00:23.384 --> 00:00:24.498
What colours?

13
00:00:24.658 --> 00:00:26.423
A quick look says 'a face'.

14
00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:32.852
A long look says 'two eyes cut through the wood, a triangle mouth, curved lines carved across the forehead'.

15
00:00:33.552 --> 00:00:34.946
The same and different.

16
00:00:35.106 --> 00:00:37.288
Put two pictures side by side.

17
00:00:37.448 --> 00:00:38.749
What do both have?

18
00:00:38.909 --> 00:00:40.255
What does only one have?

19
00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:45.199
Saying what is the same and what is different, and why, is how artists talk about art.

20
00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:46.920
Kind words.

21
00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.378
When a friend shows you their picture, say something kind about it.

22
00:00:50.538 --> 00:00:54.996
Name something that is really there: 'I like your big yellow sun.'

23
00:00:55.156 --> 00:00:58.081
That is celebrating, and every artist needs it.
